      "description": "Watch Al Riyadh vs Neom SC highlights and goals from Pro League - Saudi Arabia on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 28, 2026. The Pro League clash between Al Riyadh and Neom SC on August 28, 2026, was a testament to tactical discipline and grit. Both managers prepared their squads for a high-intensity battle where every challenge and substitution would carry significant weight in the final outcome. A Physical First Half Stalemate From the opening whistle, it was clear that neither side was willing to concede an inch of territory. The first half was characterized by a dense midfield battle and a succession of fouls that tested the referee's patience. Victor Lekhal received the game's first yellow card in the 38th minute, setting a tone for a physical encounter. As the match approached the break, the intensity only grew, with Haroune Camara and Fahad Al Jayzani both entering the book during a heated period of stoppage time, leaving the game goalless at the interval. The Tactical Pivot and Breakthrough At the start of the second half, Al Riyadh made a decisive move by introducing Hassan Al-Ali in place of Fahad Al Jayzani . This substitution proved to be the turning point of the match. While Bernard Mensah picked up a yellow card for a robust challenge in the 54th minute, the momentum was shifting. In the 61st minute, the deadlock was finally broken. Hassan Al-Ali turned provider, delivering a perfect ball for Teddy Okou , who kept his composure to fire the ball home and give his side the lead. Game Management and the Final Whistle Following the goal, both teams turned to their benches to influence the final stages. Trezeguet and Khalifah Al-Dawsari were among those replaced as the managers looked to adjust their shapes for the closing twenty minutes. Teddy Okou , the hero of the night, was given a rest in the 82nd minute as Marzouq Tambakti came on to shore up the defense. Despite late pressure and multiple substitutions from Neom SC , including the introduction of Faisel Al-Ghamdi , Al Riyadh held firm. The referee blew the final whistle at 90+6, confirming a hard-fought victory."
